The autoscaler is the glue between the policy engine (W10) and the pool's Resize methods (W09).

```go
type Autoscaler struct {
    policy    Policy
    pool      *agent.Pool
    collector *metrics.Collector
    interval  time.Duration
    logger    *slog.Logger
}

func (a *Autoscaler) Run(ctx context.Context) error {
    ticker := time.NewTicker(a.interval)
    defer ticker.Stop()
    for {
        select {
        case <-ctx.Done():
            return ctx.Err()
        case <-ticker.C:
            sys := a.collector.Latest()
            pool := a.pool.Metrics()
            decision := a.policy.Evaluate(sys, pool)
            a.apply(decision)
        }
    }
}
```

The apply method calls pool.ScaleUp or pool.ScaleDown based on the decision. It logs every scaling event with the decision's reason and confidence. If scaling fails (e.g., already at max), it logs a warning.

Wire into cmd/samverk/main.go: start the autoscaler goroutine alongside the dispatcher when scaling is enabled in config. When disabled, the pool behaves exactly as today (fixed workers).

Also emit scaling events as structured log entries that can be queried later (Phase 4).
